# PROVENANCE - nonfree/brcm43455

Cypress/Broadcom CYW43455 radio firmware, for the Raspberry Pi 4 Model B's onboard WiFi.

**Why this is here at all, and why it is not source.** This part contains its own processor and RAM with
no ROM firmware for the MAC: until a host uploads code into it there is no 802.11 inside to talk to. The
register-level interface to the radio is not published - only the protocol you speak to the firmware once
it runs. So these files are the program for a second CPU, and nobody writes them. Not Linux, not the Pi's
own boot firmware, not Windows. See `docs/wifi.md` section 8.

**Licence.** `LICENCE` in this directory, fetched with the files. It permits redistribution in binary
form with the copyright notice attached - which is what that file is - and explicitly forbids any attempt
to modify, reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble. GodspeedOS does none of those: it uploads them to
the device and speaks the documented protocol.

**Retrieved** 2026-09-27 from `RPi-Distro/firmware-nonfree`, branch `bookworm`. That repository is Debian
PACKAGING SOURCE rather than the installed layout, which is why the paths below are not the names the
files carry here: the board-specific `brcmfmac43455-sdio.raspberrypi,4-model-b.*` names upstream are
symlinks into `cypress/`, and the unsuffixed `.bin` name is produced by the packaging rules at build
time. The files are stored here under the names the driver loads; the SHA-256 is of the CONTENT, so a
